.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
.TH RELIQUARYD 1 "" "reliquary @version@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reliquaryd \- Reliquary per\-user token daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reliquaryd
.RB [ \-v | \-vv ]
.RB [ \-\-store
.IR path ]
.br
.B reliquaryd
.BR \-\-help | \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B reliquaryd
is the per\-user daemon at the center of Reliquary. It guards the user's token
store and performs every private\-key operation itself, exposing them to
clients over an Assuan control socket. It never hands key material back out:
.BR reliquary\-tool (1),
the PKCS#11 module, and the GnuPG scdaemon proxy all connect to it and ask it
to sign, decrypt, or authenticate.
.PP
The daemon runs as the invoking user and is installed setgid
.BR @group@ ,
which grants it access to the store root while DAC keeps each user confined to
their own subtree. It is normally started on demand through systemd socket
activation rather than run by hand.
.PP
Each client connection is served by a forked child, and all session state
lives in that child and dies with the connection, so the long\-lived parent
caches no key material. The daemon runs until it is stopped or killed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-vv
Increase log verbosity by one or two levels. The effective level is the
greater of this and
.BR RELIQUARY_DEBUG .
.TP
.BI "\-\-store " path
Serve the store rooted at
.I path
instead of the default
.IR @store_dir@/<uid>/ .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Required. The control socket is created at
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/reliquary/socket .
.TP
.B RELIQUARY_DEBUG
Numeric log level applied when higher than the
.BR \-v / \-vv
flags.
.TP
.BR LISTEN_FDS ", " LISTEN_PID
Set by systemd socket activation. When present, the daemon serves the
inherited socket instead of creating its own.
.TP
.BR RELIQUARY_SKIP_SETGID_CHECK ", " RELIQUARY_SKIP_SECCOMP ", " RELIQUARY_SKIP_LANDLOCK
Bypass the setgid self\-check, the seccomp filter, or the Landlock
confinement respectively. Intended only for development and testing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/reliquary/socket
Assuan control socket clients connect to (its directory is mode 0700).
.TP
.I @store_dir@/<uid>/
Per\-user token store served by default.
.SH SECURITY
.B reliquaryd
must be installed setgid
.BR @group@ ,
mode 2755
.BR root:@group@ ,
and refuses to start otherwise. At startup it installs a seccomp system\-call
filter (refusing to start if the kernel cannot apply one), confines its
filesystem access to the served store with Landlock where available, marks
itself non\-dumpable and no\-new\-privileges, and clamps its umask to 0077. The
skip variables above defeat these protections and exist only for the test
suite.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Exits 0 for
.BR \-\-help ;
otherwise it runs until terminated by a signal. It exits non\-zero, without
serving, when it refuses to start \- an unset
.BR XDG_RUNTIME_DIR ,
a failed setgid check, an unavailable seccomp filter, or a socket it cannot
create \- and on an unknown option.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR reliquary\-tool (1),
.BR reliquary\-setup\-user (8),
.BR systemd.socket (5)
